                    "text": "I now have the full picture. Let me state the root cause precisely before fixing.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`AnimaClipsData` uses a **normalized weight blend**: `RootMixer` mixes move / attack / common, and `AttackMixer` mixes attack / end. The final pose is a weighted average, so the weights on both mixers must always sum to 1 and every port must always hold a valid playable.\n\nBoth requirements are violated:\n\n**1. `StartAttackEnd` disconnects the end port before connecting the new one** (AnimaClipsData.cs:210-218). `AttackMixer` has 2 ports. `graph.Disconnect(AttackMixer, attackEndInputPort)` leaves port 1 empty, and an empty port in `AnimationMixerPlayable` contributes the **rest pose (T-pose)**, not \"nothing\". So during the frames between that disconnect and the connect — and during the frames while `UpdateBlend` ramps `RootMixer` weight 1 up from ~0 to 1 (blendSpeed 8 means several frames at ~0.1-0.5) — the attack branch is blended in at a *partial* weight against a degenerate/empty pose. That is your one-frame T-pose flash.\n\n**2. `PlayAttackClip` resets the wrong playables.** It calls `ResetAttackAnimationTime(attackInputPort)` and `ResetAttackAnimationTime(attackEndInputPort)` **before** connecting anything (AnimaClipsData.cs:177-181). At that moment the port holds either nothing (first attack) or the *previous* combo's stale playable. The freshly created `CachedAttackClipPlayable` / `CachedEndClipPlayable` are never reset, so the end clip enters at an arbitrary leftover time. Combined with #1, the end animation pops.\n\n**3. Disconnect/reconnect churn.** `CachedAttackClipPlayable` gets rebuilt on every combo hit, and `SetClip` is never used, so graph topology is destroyed and rebuilt each attack — that is what makes the degenerate-window possible in the first place.\n\n## The fix\n\nKeep both attack ports **permanently connected** to persistent `AnimationClipPlayable`s and swap only the clip asset plus weights via `SetClip`. Weight changes happen in the same frame, with the incoming port weighted before the outgoing one is zeroed.\n\nLet me apply it."
